Public re-injection of the radio IRQ event (calls the registered RAC
irq callback exactly as the GPIO ISR would have). The transceiver
event pin interrupt is edge-triggered while the chip holds its IRQ
line high until serviced over SPI; an edge lost in a disabled window
stalls the awaiting transaction forever. The application main loop
polls the pin level and calls this when it observes the interrupt
undelivered. Idempotent when no IRQ is pending.
---
 modules/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.c b/modules/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.c
index ef24d8b..86d03b6 100644
--- a/modules/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.c
+++ b/modules/smtc_modem_hal/smtc_modem_hal.c
@@ -329,6 +329,28 @@ void smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_clear_pending( void )
     prv_radio_irq_pending_while_disabled      = false;
 }
 
+void smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_kick( void )
+{
+    /* LOST-EDGE RESUSCITATION: the transceiver's event pin interrupt is
+     * EDGE-triggered (see lr20xx_board.c), and the chip holds its IRQ
+     * line HIGH until the mask is cleared over SPI. An edge that fires
+     * while the GPIO interrupt is momentarily disabled — the RAC
+     * reconfigures the radio across transaction boundaries, exactly when
+     * the peer's phase-aligned frame arrives — is lost forever: the pin
+     * stays high, no further edge can occur, and the transaction's
+     * completion or the received packet is never surfaced (bench
+     * 2026-08-25: chip demod counted the packets — hwrx grew — while the
+     * app saw nothing, in both TX (hung burst) and RX (eaten vote) form).
+     * The main loop calls this periodically: if the event pin is still
+     * HIGH, the interrupt the chip is asserting was never delivered —
+     * re-inject it here. Safe by construction: the RAC's irq processing
+     * is idempotent when no IRQ is actually pending. */
+    if( prv_modem_irq_enabled && prv_smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_callback != NULL )
+    {
+        prv_smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_callback( prv_smtc_modem_hal_radio_irq_context );
+    }
+}
+
 bool smtc_modem_external_stack_currently_use_radio( void )
 {
     /* return false if the radio is available for the lbm stack
